      "inputTokens": 101,
      "outputTokens": 851,
      "costUsd": 0.0077095,
      "pronunciationText": "First, why is this geometric? Each year, the population is multiplied by the same factor. Growing by five per cent means keeping all one hundred per cent, and adding five more. So each value is multiplied by one point zero five. Falling by twenty per cent means keeping eighty per cent, so r is zero point eight. Either way, every period multiplies by the same number, so the values make a geometric sequence. Arithmetic models add the same amount. Geometric models multiply by the same factor."
    },
