      "pronunciationText": "Now the timing. Call the starting amount A, at time zero. After one period, it's A times r. After t periods, it's been multiplied t times, so the amount is A, times r to the t. Time is in the power, so the quantity is an exponential function of time. In sequence language, the start is the first term, so after t periods we're at term t plus one. Some questions call the value after the first period the first term instead. Then after t periods, you're at term t. So always ask what time the first term is."
