      "pronunciationText": "When does a chain message reach a million people? Five hundred people have it at the start, and the number who have it triples every hour. Set five hundred times three to the t above one million. Divide by five hundred, so three to the t is more than two thousand. Take logs, and divide by log three, which is positive, so the inequality stays the same way round. Then t is more than about six point nine two. So seven is the first whole hour with more than a million. Check: after six hours it's three hundred and sixty-four thousand, five hundred, and after seven, one million, ninety-three thousand, five hundred."
