      "costUsd": 0.011674,
      "pronunciationText": "Now decay. A camper trailer costs thirty thousand dollars new, and loses fifteen per cent of its value each year. So r is zero point eight five, and after n years it's worth thirty thousand, times zero point eight five to the n. After five years, that's about thirteen thousand three hundred and eleven dollars. When is it first worth less than ten thousand? Divide by thirty thousand, so zero point eight five to the n is less than a third. Take logs. But log of zero point eight five is negative, and dividing by a negative number flips the inequality. So n is more than about six point seven six, and the answer is seven years. Check: after six years it's worth about eleven thousand three hundred dollars, and after seven, about nine thousand six hundred."
