      "pronunciationText": "Compare that with an arithmetic model. If the trailer lost a fixed four thousand five hundred dollars every year, which is fifteen per cent of its first price, it would be worth nothing after six and two thirds years. The geometric model takes fifteen per cent of what's left, so each year's loss is smaller than the one before. Its value gets closer and closer to zero, but never reaches it."
