      "costUsd": 0.0104645,
      "pronunciationText": "An oil well produces fifty thousand barrels in its first year, and each year after that, ten per cent less than the year before. Here the first term is the first year's output, so year n is term n. So ay is fifty thousand, and r is zero point nine. Over the first ten years, the well produces S ten. That's fifty thousand, times one minus zero point nine to the ten, over zero point one, which is about three hundred and twenty-five thousand, six hundred and sixty-one barrels. And since r is less than one, the totals settle. S infinity is fifty thousand over zero point one, which is five hundred thousand. However long it runs, the well can never produce more than five hundred thousand barrels."
